<figure id="A11.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Mapping of display columns in results tables to MMD configurations. For all RBF MMDs, the final MMD was computed as the maximum value over the following bandwidths <math id="A11.T14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{6}=\{0.1,0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0,10.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}_{i=1}^{6}=\{0.1,0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0,10.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> as per <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Thompson et al. (2022)</a></cite>. For the descriptor parameters, we used 100,000 for the width of the sparse degree histogram, 100 bins for the clustering histogram, and 4 for the orbit count. RBF: radial basis function; GTV: Gaussian total variation distance; UMVE: unbiased minimum variance estimator, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gretton et al. (2012)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
