<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>Stability of PolyGraph Discrepancy under varying sample sizes.</h3>

<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A12.F23" title="In Appendix L Stability of PolyGraph Discrepancy under varying sample sizes. ‣ Appendix ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, <a href="#A12.F24" title="Figure 24 ‣ Appendix L Stability of PolyGraph Discrepancy under varying sample sizes. ‣ Appendix ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, <a href="#A12.F25" title="Figure 25 ‣ Appendix L Stability of PolyGraph Discrepancy under varying sample sizes. ‣ Appendix ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> and <a href="#A12.F26" title="Figure 26 ‣ Appendix L Stability of PolyGraph Discrepancy under varying sample sizes. ‣ Appendix ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> show the relationship between the PolyGraph Discrepancy score and the number of samples. The PolyGraph Discrepancy score of the reference graphs with respect to another set of reference graphs issued from the same distribution is given as a comparison. For all experiments, we show the mean as well as the 5<sup id="A12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">th</sup> and 95<sup id="A12.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">th</sup> quantile to give an estimate of the variance of PolyGraph Discrepancy at different sample sizes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For most models, some separation from the test set occurs above <math id="A12.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> samples, with PolyGraph Discrepancy scores, and especially the upper bound is mostly stable beyond this range. This both showcases the stability of the metric, the number of samples required to get a reliable PolyGraph Discrepancy estimate, as well as the overall PGD ranges for the various models we considered for this study.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A12.F23" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06122v1/autograph_pgs_subsampling.svg" id="A12.F23.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/273;" width="548" height="273"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 23: </span>PolyGraph Discrepancy obtained from varying sample sizes generated by AutoGraph.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A12.F24" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06122v1/digress_pgs_subsampling.svg" id="A12.F24.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/272;" width="548" height="272"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 24: </span>PolyGraph Discrepancy obtained from varying sample sizes generated by <span id="A12.F24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DiGress</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A12.F25" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06122v1/gran_pgs_subsampling.svg" id="A12.F25.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/272;" width="548" height="272"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 25: </span>PolyGraph Discrepancy obtained from varying sample sizes generated by GRAN.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A12.F26" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06122v1/esgg_pgs_subsampling.svg" id="A12.F26.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/272;" width="548" height="272"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 26: </span>PolyGraph Discrepancy obtained from varying sample sizes generated by ESGG.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A13" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix M </span>Larger Procedural Reference Datasets for Better graph generative model Benchmarking</h3>

<div id="A13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following our findings of <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 High Bias and Variance plague MMD-based graph generative model Benchmarks ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Supplemental for: High Bias and Variance Plague MMD-based GGM Benchmarks ‣ Appendix ‣ PolyGraph Discrepancy: a classifier-based metric for graph generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>, we introduce larger procedurally-generated datasets for planar, lobster and SBM graphs, which we term <span id="A13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Planar-L</span>, <span id="A13.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Lobster-L</span> and <span id="A13.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SBM-L</span>. <span id="A13.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Lobster-L</span> is a set of tree-shaped lobster graphs generated using <code id="A13.p1.1.5" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">nx.random_lobster</code>, controlled by expected node count (<math id="A13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math>) and attachment probabilities to the backbone and its neighbors (set to <math id="A13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math> for both). <span id="A13.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Planar-L</span> is a set of connected planar graphs generated by uniformly sampling <math id="A13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> node positions in the unit square and forming the Delaunay triangulation via <code id="A13.p1.1.7" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">scipy.spatial.Delaunay</code>, yielding planar edge sets from triangle simplices. <span id="A13.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SBM-L</span> is a set of stochastic block model graphs with the number of communities sampled uniformly from <math id="A13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> and nodes per community from <math id="A13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math>, where edges are drawn with intra-community probability <math id="A13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3</annotation></semantics></math> and inter-community probability <math id="A13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.005</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.005</annotation></semantics></math>. SBM-L, <span id="A13.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Planar-L</span>, and <span id="A13.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Lobster-L</span> datasets follow <span id="A13.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">networkx</span>’s BSD-3 license.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A13.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span>Dataset sizes (number of graphs) per split.</figcaption>
